","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:3d7cea0d8243035f9aff06289eeead41503fc9880478cbcd313207989c39e8d0","file":"preprints/The-free-uniform-spanning-forest-is-a-factor-of-IID-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":124,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"70044def45367c5a48ee1906457f558be7e856e5106bf4af2299ab89dd8782ee","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-free-uniform-spanning-forest-is-a-factor-of-IID-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:3d7cea0d8243035f9aff06289eeead41503fc9880478cbcd313207989c39e8d0","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-free-uniform-spanning-forest-is-a-factor-of-IID-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L124"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:dpp-group}\nLet $\\Gamma$ be a countable group and let $K$ be a self-adjoint positive\ncontraction on $\\ell^2(\\Gamma)$, so $0\\le K\\le I$. If the determinantal\nprobability law with kernel $K$ is invariant under the regular left action,\nthen it is a factor of IID under that action. In particular, this holds\nwhenever $K$ commutes with the left regular representation of $\\Gamma$."}
